  <h2>1. avaTOK is a venue, not a party to your deal</h2>
  <p>
    When a buyer purchases a digital service from a seller, the contract for that service is
    <strong>between the buyer and the seller</strong>. avaTOK provides the marketplace, the tools,
    and the payment rails. We are not the seller, not the buyer, not an agent for either, and not a
    party to the transaction.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not guarantee the quality, legality, safety, or accuracy of any listing, and we do not
    guarantee that a buyer will pay or that a seller will deliver. We may verify certain
    information about sellers, but unless a listing expressly says otherwise, assume we have not
    verified a seller's skills, credentials, or claims.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Seller eligibility and responsibilities</h2>
  <p>To sell on avaTOK you must:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Be of legal age to enter a contract where you live, and have an account in good
      standing.</li>
    <li>Complete any identity, tax, or payout verification we require before you can be paid.</li>
    <li>Hold every licence, registration, or permission your service needs in your jurisdiction and
      in the buyer's, and keep them current.</li>
    <li>Be responsible for your own taxes. You are responsible for determining, collecting where
      applicable, reporting, and paying any taxes on your earnings, including GST in India. We may
      collect tax information from you and may withhold or report amounts where the law requires
      it.</li>
    <li>Comply with all laws that apply to what you are selling, including consumer protection,
      advertising, export, and data protection law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You are solely responsible for what you list, what you promise, and what you deliver.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Accurate listings</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Describe what the buyer actually gets: the scope, the format, what is included and what is
      not.</li>
    <li>State the price, delivery time, and any revision policy clearly before purchase.</li>
    <li>Do not use misleading titles, fake reviews, borrowed portfolios, or samples you did not
      create.</li>
    <li>Do not claim a qualification, certification, award, or affiliation you do not hold.</li>
    <li>Disclose where AI tools do a substantial part of the work, if a reasonable buyer would want
      to know.</li>
    <li>Keep listings up to date and pause them if you cannot deliver.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Delivering the service</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Deliver through avaTOK, within the time you stated, and to the scope you described.</li>
    <li>Communicate on the platform. Taking a deal off-platform to avoid fees removes the buyer's
      protections and may lead to enforcement.</li>
    <li>If you cannot deliver, say so promptly so the order can be cancelled or refunded — see
      <a href="/refunds">Refunds &amp; Cancellations</a>.</li>
    <li>Do not ask a buyer to pay outside avaTOK, and do not request payment by methods we do not
      support.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Buyer responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read the listing before you buy and ask questions if the scope is not clear.</li>
    <li>Give the seller what they need — briefs, files, access, feedback — on time.</li>
    <li>Do not use a seller's work outside the licence you were granted, and do not resell it as
      your own where that was not part of the deal.</li>
    <li>Do not use the marketplace to obtain anything prohibited by our
      <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>.</li>
    <li>Do not abuse cancellations, refunds, or chargebacks. Filing a chargeback instead of using
      our dispute process may result in account action.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Prohibited listings</h2>
  <p>You may not list, and may not buy:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Anything illegal, or anything requiring a licence you do not hold.</li>
    <li>Adult or sexual services of any kind. Anything involving a minor is absolutely prohibited —
      see <a href="/child-safety">Child Safety Standards</a>.</li>
    <li>Academic work presented as the buyer's own where that breaches an institution's rules, and
      other services designed to deceive third parties.</li>
    <li>Fake engagement, followers, reviews, ratings, or traffic, on avaTOK or anywhere else.</li>
    <li>Hacking, account access, data scraping, malware, or anything designed to compromise
      systems, accounts, or privacy.</li>
    <li>Content or software you do not have the right to sell, including pirated material and
      leaked databases — see <a href="/dmca">DMCA / Copyright</a>.</li>
    <li>Regulated advice — medical, legal, financial — offered without the licences and disclosures
      the law requires. See the <a href="/consultation-terms">Live Consultation Terms</a>.</li>
    <li>Money transfer, currency exchange, lending, investment schemes, or anything that
      functions as a financial service.</li>
    <li>Personal data about other people, and identity or verification documents.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Fees and commission</h2>
  <p>
    avaTOK charges a commission on marketplace sales, and payment processors may charge their own
    fees. The rates that apply to you, and how they are shown at checkout, are set out on our
    <a href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a> page. We may change fees; we will publish
    changes before they take effect, and changes do not apply retroactively to orders already
    placed.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Payments and payouts</h2>
  <p>
    Buyer payments are collected through our payment providers. Seller earnings are held and
    released according to our <a href="/payouts">Payouts</a> policy, which sets out clearing
    periods, minimum thresholds, supported methods, and the information you must provide to be
    paid. We may hold, delay, or reverse a payout where we suspect fraud, a chargeback, a policy
    violation, or where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Cancellations, refunds, and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    Cancellation and refund rules are on our <a href="/refunds">Refunds &amp; Cancellations</a>
    page.
  </p>
  <p>
    A dispute about a digital service is fundamentally between the buyer and the seller, and you
    should try to resolve it directly first. If you cannot, you can raise it with us. We may, at
    our discretion, review the order, look at what was delivered, and decide how funds held on the
    platform are released — including refunding the buyer in whole or in part, or releasing payment
    to the seller. <strong>Our role is limited.</strong> We are not an arbitrator, our decision is
    about the funds we hold and nothing more, and it does not stop either party pursuing whatever
    legal rights they have against the other.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Our right to remove listings and accounts</h2>
  <p>
    We may remove, hide, edit the visibility of, or refuse any listing, and we may limit or
    terminate a seller or buyer account, at our discretion — for example where a listing breaks
    these terms or the law, where we receive credible reports, where a rights holder complains, or
    where we need to protect users or the platform. Where it is practical and lawful, we will tell
    you why and you can appeal to
    <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Intellectual property and licences</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your listing content stays yours.</strong> By listing, you grant avaTOK a
      non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free licence to host, display, reproduce, and promote your
      listing content — titles, descriptions, images, samples, video — for the purpose of operating
      and marketing the marketplace. This licence ends when you remove the listing, except for
      copies in backups, records we must keep, and material already used in published promotion.</li>
    <li><strong>What the buyer gets</strong> is what the listing says. If the listing does not
      specify, the buyer receives a licence to use the delivered work for the purpose described in
      the order, and the seller keeps ownership.</li>
    <li>You warrant that you own or are licensed to use everything you upload, and that it does not
      infringe anyone's rights.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>12. No employment relationship</h2>
  <p>
    Sellers are independent. Nothing here creates an employment, agency, partnership, joint
    venture, or franchise relationship between a seller and avaTOK, or between a seller and a
    buyer. Sellers control how, when, and where they work, set their own prices within the
    marketplace, and are responsible for their own equipment, insurance, benefits, and taxes.
    avaTOK does not supervise or direct a seller's work.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, avaTOK is not liable for the acts or omissions of any
    buyer or seller, for the quality or legality of any service, or for losses arising from a
    transaction between users. The limitations and exclusions in our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> apply to these Marketplace Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. We will post the updated version here and revise the date above.
    Continuing to buy or sell after a change means you accept it.
  </p>

  <p>
    Questions? Email <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>. Users in India can
    also use our <a href="/grievance">Grievance Redressal</a> process.
  </p>
